# Celestial Armor has flash: on Bot2's turn 2, with Lightning Bolt aimed at Elvish Mystic on the stack, Bot1 casts it. Entering, it
# attaches to the Mystic (a target chosen as the trigger goes on the stack), which gains hexproof and indestructible until end of
# turn (CR 702.11b, 702.12b): the Bolt's target is now illegal and it fizzles (CR 608.2b), so the Mystic takes nothing. Equipped it is a 3/1 with flying (+2/+0).
# On turn 3 the "until end of turn" part is over: the Mystic keeps flying (from the Armor) but is no longer hexproof or indestructible.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Elvish Mystic
Celestial Armor
Island
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Celestial Armor.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic.Keywords = Flying; Hexproof; Indestructible
? Bot1.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic.Power = 3
? Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
[T3 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Celestial Armor.AttachedTo = Elvish Mystic
Bot1.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic.Keywords = Flying
Bot1.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic.Power = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic.Damage = 0
